  set:  # 0a19
    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per discussion surrounding WI-votut. See sister item `WI-mifif` (Django) — the first-framework PR.\n\n## Gap\n\n`hypergumbo run` on a Phoenix app produces no `renders` edge connecting a controller action to its template file. The implicit `MyAppWeb.UserController.show/2` → `lib/my_app_web/templates/user/show.html.{eex,heex,leex}` relationship is not captured.\n\n`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/phoenix_ipc.py` exists but covers a different concern (PubSub channels / GenServer dispatch), not view-template binding.\n\n## Phoenix convention to model\n\n- **Action detection**: any function in a `*Controller` module that takes `(conn, params)` (Phoenix 1.x) or any function annotated with `@action` (Phoenix 1.7+).\n- **Module / module-attribute markers**: `use Phoenix.Controller, ...`, `defmodule MyAppWeb.UserController`.\n- **Template path derivation**:\n  - Phoenix 1.x: `MyAppWeb.UserController` action `show` → `lib/my_app_web/templates/user/show.html.{eex,heex}` (controller name strips `Controller`, snake_cases, looks up under `templates/`).\n  - Phoenix 1.7+: HEEx `.heex` is the default; templates are co-located with views in `lib/my_app_web/controllers/user_html/show.html.heex` (function-component shape).\n- **Extensions**: `.html.eex`, `.html.heex`, `.html.leex`, `.text.eex`, `.json.eex`, `.xml.eex`.\n- **Out of scope**: Phoenix LiveView (`*_live.ex`) uses inline templates inside the LiveView module, not separate template files. Different shape, separate linker if ever needed.\n\n## Strategy alignment with shared core\n\nThis linker uses the **method/class-name strategy** exposed by the shared core extracted in WI-mifif (same family as Rails and Django CBV defaults). The controller module name + action name + Phoenix 1.x vs 1.7+ resolution rules become a thin `PhoenixStrategy` class against the shared probe-and-emit loop. No new strategy class needed at the core level — this is the second consumer of an already-extracted hook.\n\n## Build order\n\nBlocked on WI-mifif merging (shared core extraction). Once WI-mifif lands, this is implementable independently of WI-hogik/WI-hokaj.\n\n## Analyzer pre-req\n\nConfirm before scheduling: the Elixir analyzer correctly extracts `defmodule MyAppWeb.UserController` + function names + `use Phoenix.Controller` markers. Sibling lang-mainstream/lang-common analyzer capability could bottleneck.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A Phoenix fixture with `MyAppWeb.UserController.show/2` and `lib/my_app_web/templates/user/show.html.eex` produces a `renders` edge.\n- Phoenix 1.7 function-component shape (`UserHTML.show/1` + `controllers/user_html/show.html.heex`) is also handled.\n- 100% coverage on changed source."  # 0a19
